   "source": [
    "#| echo: false\n",
    "#| output: asis\n",
    "import json\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "rows = []\n",
    "for f in sorted(Path(\"notebooks/timings\").glob(\"*.json\")):\n",
    "    rows += json.loads(f.read_text())\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "lines = [\"| Case | Rows → summary | Wall time | Speed-up | Min ESS/s |\", \"|---|---|---|---|---|\"]\n",
    "for case, g in df.groupby(\"case\", sort=False):\n",
    "    raw = g[g.kind == \"raw\"].iloc[0]\n",
    "    for _, comp in g[g.kind != \"raw\"].iterrows():\n",
    "        label = case if comp.kind == \"compressed\" else f\"{case}, re-centred\"\n",
    "        lines.append(f\"| {label} | {raw.rows:,} → {comp.rows:,} | {raw.wall_s:.1f}s → {comp.wall_s:.1f}s | \"\n",
    "                     f\"{raw.wall_s / comp.wall_s:.0f}× | {raw.min_ess_per_s:,.0f} → {comp.min_ess_per_s:,.0f} |\")\n",
    "print(\"\\n\".join(lines))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "149dc87d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Practical notes\n",
    "\n",
    "Run row-level checks before compressing. Compression removes the rows those checks need. You can keep a raw-data\n",
    "model, fitted to a sample, for diagnostics.\n",
    "\n",
    "Use an observed distribution rather than `pm.Potential` when one exists. `Binomial`, `Multinomial`, `Poisson`, the\n",
    "Normal–Gamma pair for $(\\bar y, SS)$ and the Gaussian pseudo-observation all keep a pointwise log-likelihood, so\n",
    "leave-one-out cross-validation still works. It now works at the level of the cell rather than the individual. The\n",
    "Gram-matrix model is the one case here that needs a `Potential`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Counts, exposures and Gram matrices are additive. They can be summed across days, partitions or machines. This makes\n",
    "them well suited to streaming data and to data held in a warehouse, where the summaries can be computed in SQL.\n",
    "\n",
    "Approximate summaries depend on their expansion point. They are accurate near that point and less accurate far from it.\n",
    "Summaries computed around different expansion points cannot be added together.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each summary also states an assumption of the model. Writing down $(n, k)$ says which users are interchangeable.\n",
    "Writing down $(d, r)$ says which covariates define a risk set. Writing down $N_{ij}$ says that the next step depends only\n",
    "on the current state. If one of those statements is false for your data, the compressed model is wrong in the same way\n",
    "the full model is, and it is cheaper to find out by checking the statement directly.\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebooks are in the [project folder](https://github.com/NathanielF/NathanielF.github.io/tree/master/posts/post-with-code/SufficientStatistics).\n",
    "I plan to add more cases."
   ]
  }
 ],
